This death regression includes one mutable physical header in two distinct
lexical scopes under different macro definitions.  The transformation
therefore produces two non-equivalent typed lexical subtrees for one physical
output file.

The header planner must reject that contradiction from canonical AST
properties, edges, types, symbols, and source identity.  It must not compare
unparsed strings, and it must continue to accept repeated occurrences whose
typed lexical subtrees are equivalent.
